<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iqta</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Iqtadari</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The iqta was an Islamic administrative system in which the right to collect revenue from a territory was assigned to military officers in place of salary. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Empire</a> used it widely to support its armies. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a> adopted it as the basis of its revenue and military organisation.</p></div>
